Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Hainaut, Donatien
Author-Email: donatien.hainaut(at)uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, LIDAM/ISBA, Belgium
Title: American option pricing with model constrained Gaussian process regressions
Abstract: This article introduces a novel method based on Gaussian process regression for pricing American options. The variational partial differential equation (PDE) governing option prices is converted into a non-linear penalized Feynman-Kac equation (PFK). We propose an iterative algorithm to manage the non-linearity of the PFK operator. We sample state variables in the PDE’s inner domain and on the terminal boundary. At each step, we fit a constrained regression function approximating the option price. This function matches the option payoffs on the boundary sample while satisfying the PFK PDE on the inner sample. The non-linear term in this PDE is frozen and valued with the price estimate from the previous iteration. We adopt a Bayesian framework in which payoffs and the value of the FK PDE in the boundary and inner samples are noised. Assuming the regression function is a Gaussian process, we find a closed-form approximation of option prices. In the numerical illustration, we evaluate American put options in the Heston model and in the two-factor Hull-White model.
Keywords: Gaussian process regression ; American option pricing ; Feynman-Kac equation ; Heston model
Length: 23
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, ISBA
Number: 2024023
Creation-Date: 2024-10-16
File-URL: https://dial.uclouvain.be/pr/boreal/en/object/boreal%3A292665/datastream/PDF_01/view
